{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 123, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 absent the output depends only on edges 3 and 5, so adding a conv on edge 3 adds an essential path, sometimes reconnecting the output (exp 3, 4 vs 1, 2)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is already missing leaves node 3 with few or no inputs, so the edit is far more harmful (exp 72, 74 vs 71, 73)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the input-to-output edge 3 is absent, deleting edge 4 removes one of the few remaining paths into the output (exp 42, 44 vs 41, 43)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without edge 3, edge 5 carries a larger share of the signal into the output, and it can reconnect a cell whose output was cut off (exp 17 vs 11-16, 18-20)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on edge 4 matters much more when the direct edge 3 is missing, since it may be the only output path (exp 93 vs 91, 95, 96)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip-dominated cells lack learnable capacity, so adding a 3x3 conv to them yields large gains, whereas conv-rich cells barely improve (exp 28, 29 vs 21-27)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Inserting a conv into a parameter-free all-skip cell gives a huge improvement compared with conv-rich parents (exp 85 vs 11-20)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing edge 1's conv with pooling is nearly harmless when edge 0 still provides a conv, but catastrophic when it removes the only conv in a skip or pool cell (exp 51-53, 56-58, 60 vs 54, 59)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Adding another 3x3 conv shows diminishing returns in cells already containing 3x3 convs, versus large gains in skip or 1x1 cells (exp 61-67, 70 vs 68, 69)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 4 hurts more when it removes a 3x3 conv than when it removes a skip, pool or 1x1 op (exp 41-45, 49, 50 vs 46-48)."}], "tok": 17584, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_con